WEBVTT

00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:12.300
<v Tomasz Nowak>Morning, everyone. Monday again. Can you all hear me? Right, let's do nights first, then what's actually on the list.</v>

00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:21.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, got you. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid. I've spent longer looking at the same van than I have at this screen.</v>

00:00:22.329 --> 00:00:30.730
<v Jamie Brennan>Lovely start. We were making weekend plans yesterday, thinking we'd get out walking next weekend. Seen the weather now, though. Probably another weekend indoors.</v>

00:00:32.859 --> 00:00:40.909
<v Priya Raman>At least indoors might have coffee. The broken coffee machine in the canteen is still doing its impression of a very expensive cupboard.</v>

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.719
<v Tomasz Nowak>So morale's excellent, then.</v>

00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:49.759
<v Priya Raman>Outstanding. And that's a complaint, not me volunteering to repair it.</v>

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.009
<v Tomasz Nowak>Noted. Olu, anything carried over from last night?</v>

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:59.240
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, so, finished the repair on the GT1 fuel valve last night. That's done.</v>

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.750
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fully finished, not one of those 'done apart from' ones?</v>

00:01:06.959 --> 00:01:09.409
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Fully finished. Nothing left on that repair.</v>

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:15.879
<v Aisha Begum>Same from me: finished the repair on the GT1 compressor last night. That's closed as well.</v>

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.650
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. Neither of those needs carrying onto today's list.</v>

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.790
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly, just reporting it back.</v>

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:33.459
<v Jamie Brennan>One thing from nights, I noticed the desiccant unit was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:34.859 --> 00:01:39.409
<v Priya Raman>Settled while you were there, you mean? Not still warm when you left?</v>

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.730
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, settled while I was there. Just an observation, not raising a job for it.</v>

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:53.609
<v Sarah Okafor>And we're still waiting on parts for the booster pump. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:55.099 --> 00:01:58.599
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, that stays blocked, then. No new action against it.</v>

00:02:00.819 --> 00:02:02.569
<v Sarah Okafor>That's it. Same position, unfortunately.</v>

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:09.419
<v Tomasz Nowak>Jamie, can you chase the purchase order for the CV01 today? Low priority, but today.</v>

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:16.449
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, I can't take that today. I'm not going to promise it and then leave it sitting there.</v>

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:24.389
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fair enough. Boss, can you take that instead—chase the purchase order for the CV01 today? Still low priority.</v>

00:02:26.009 --> 00:02:31.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll take it off Jamie. I'll chase the purchase order for the CV01 today, low priority.</v>

00:02:33.979 --> 00:02:38.180
<v Jamie Brennan>Cheers, boss. So I haven't got a parallel chase on that, then.</v>

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:43.919
<v Tomasz Nowak>Correct, just boss on the CV01 purchase order. Today, low priority.</v>

00:02:45.229 --> 00:02:46.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, mine.</v>

00:02:48.729 --> 00:02:57.479
<v Olumide Adeyemi>While we're on parts, I'll go to the treatment plant to pick up the replacement parts for the IM1 hydraulic unit by Wednesday. It's urgent.</v>

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:02.400
<v Tomasz Nowak>Thanks, Olu. By Wednesday for the collection, yeah?</v>

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:10.680
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah. I'll pick them up from the treatment plant by Wednesday. I'm not including fitting them in that.</v>

00:03:11.219 --> 00:03:15.069
<v Aisha Begum>Right, useful distinction. Replacement parts coming back, not a completed repair.</v>

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:20.310
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. It's urgent, but by Wednesday is the deadline for that pickup.</v>

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.960
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. That's with Olu.</v>

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:27.210
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, someone's gone a bit Dalek. Is it just me?</v>

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:31.539
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Might be my headset. How's that?</v>

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.979
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, you're back. Much less threatening.</v>

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:42.240
<v Hannah Price>Um, I'll order spare parts for the stacker tomorrow morning. No rush on that one.</v>

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:48.629
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cheers, Pricey. That's the spare parts order, just to keep it separate from the other bits.</v>

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.900
<v Hannah Price>Yep, the order. I'll do that tomorrow morning, no rush.</v>

00:03:55.479 --> 00:04:01.430
<v Jamie Brennan>And that's separate from the CV01 purchase order chase. Two different things, before we muddle them together.</v>

00:04:03.889 --> 00:04:06.340
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, mine's spare parts for the stacker.</v>

00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:15.349
<v Tomasz Nowak>Pricey, can you also clear the jam and check the sensors on the spinner? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:21.660
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the spinner. I'll take that.</v>

00:04:23.759 --> 00:04:27.610
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, talking over you—both bits, the jam and the sensor checks?</v>

00:04:29.509 --> 00:04:33.009
<v Hannah Price>Both, yeah. Not just clear it and call it finished.</v>

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:39.370
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly. It matters but it's not urgent, so don't read that as an emergency call-out.</v>

00:04:40.269 --> 00:04:41.670
<v Hannah Price>Understood. Important, not urgent.</v>

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:48.540
<v Aisha Begum>And I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team next week. No rush on that.</v>

00:04:50.329 --> 00:04:53.829
<v Tomasz Nowak>Thanks, Aisha. Next week for the toolbox talk, no rush.</v>

00:04:54.939 --> 00:04:57.040
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, I'll organise it. That's mine.</v>

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.939
<v Sarah Okafor>A toolbox talk where Teams doesn't eat every third word would be a novelty.</v>

00:05:04.879 --> 00:05:07.329
<v Aisha Begum>Let's not set expectations too high, boss.</v>

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:14.050
<v Jamie Brennan>Same approach I'm taking with those weekend plans. Expect rain, be pleasantly surprised.</v>

00:05:14.649 --> 00:05:18.850
<v Priya Raman>I expected coffee and was unpleasantly surprised, so your system's probably better.</v>

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:24.970
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, before this becomes the breakfast complaints channel, quick check of what we've actually agreed.</v>

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.850
<v Sarah Okafor>I've got the CV01 purchase order chase instead of Jamie. Today, low priority.</v>

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:38.050
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I'll go to the treatment plant for the replacement parts for the IM1 hydraulic unit by Wednesday. It's urgent. Collection only.</v>

00:05:39.529 --> 00:05:49.329
<v Hannah Price>I'll order spare parts for the stacker tomorrow morning, no rush. And I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the spinner—it matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:54.110
<v Aisha Begum>I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team next week. No rush.</v>

00:05:56.009 --> 00:06:01.959
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. The booster pump hasn't suddenly become another action in that lot; it's still waiting on parts.</v>

00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:07.399
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Blocked until they arrive, nothing we can do in the meantime.</v>

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:13.579
<v Tomasz Nowak>And the GT1 fuel valve and GT1 compressor repairs are finished, not being handed out again.</v>

00:06:15.699 --> 00:06:21.649
<v Jamie Brennan>Desiccant unit was only an observation as well. It settled down, so nothing new from me there.</v>

00:06:23.209 --> 00:06:27.060
<v Priya Raman>And no coffee machine job. Just a factory-wide sense of loss.</v>

00:06:29.449 --> 00:06:31.550
<v Tomasz Nowak>Tragic. Right, that's us. Cheers, everyone.</v>
